{"name":"Brik Dough","hex":"#dab77f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brik","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of burek (“type of pastry”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brik"},{"term":"dough","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick, malleable substance made by mixing flour with other ingredients such as water, eggs, or butter, that is made into a particular form and then baked.","Money."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make into dough."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dough"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brik","blocks":[{"text":"Brik or burek is the North African version of borek, a stuffed malsouka pastry which is commonly deep fried. The best-known version is the egg brik, a whole egg in a triangular pastry pocket with chopped onion, tuna, harissa and parsley. With a slightly different shape, but with identical ingredients and method of preparation, the brik is known in Algeria and Libya as bourek (بوراك). It is often filled with a raw egg and herbs or tuna, harissa and olives and is sometimes served in a pita. This is also known as a boreeka. It is also widespread in Eastern Algeria in the cities of Annaba and Costantina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Brikdish.jpg/330px-Brikdish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brik","wikidata":"Q916971"},{"title":"Dough","blocks":[{"text":"Dough is a malleable, sometimes elastic paste most commonly made from flour or meal. Dough is typically made by mixing flour with a small amount of water or other liquid, and sometimes includes yeast, other leavening agents, or ingredients such as fats or flavourings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Dough.jpg/330px-Dough.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dough","wikidata":"Q178024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG/500px-Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG/1280px-Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG/500px-Servant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A statue of a servant kneading dough, from Egypt, Old Kingdom, 5th Dynasty, c. 2494–2345 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AServant_kneading_dough%2C_Egypt%2C_Old_Kingdom%2C_5th_Dynasty%2C_c._2494-2345_BCE_-_Nelson-Atkins_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC08067.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg/500px-Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg/1280px-Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg/500px-Paratha_Peda%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org